            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/ijc.IJC_136_17</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The management of advanced nonsmall cell lung cancer (NSCLC) patients is becoming complex with the identification of driver mutations and targeted therapies. The expert group of academic medical oncologists used data from published literature, practical experience to arrive at practical consensus recommendations to treat advanced NSCLC for use by the community oncologists.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
